Z||000034||artherd||04-08-2001||08:28 PM||||I just had a thought, tina how fast were you (or rather, your rear wheels) going at the time this happened?  I wonder, because it seems the transmission is split on the wrong side (bottom as installed in a fiero) for it to be engine torque to have caused it...<P>My theroy is that the clutch... well, totally melted dudette  (rule  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and that it basically went from slipping at 6000/5000rpm, to dead stop, in a few milliseconds.<P>The rest of the driveline and/or car was still turning, and that pinpoint confinment and release of kenetic angular momentum split your case backwards-style. <P>In any event, "heh, cool"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.||||reg||3
